        "content": "## 10.8 Dynamic Routing\nDynamic Routing allows URLs to contain parameters.\n> 🚀 **Example:** /student/101 /student/102 /student/103 Route: <Route path=\"/student/:id\" element={<Student/>} /> Access Parameter: import { useParams } from \"react-router-dom\"; const { id } = useParams();",
